WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.732 --> 00:00:04.453
Danny: We’ve got to find a way to see in!

2
00:00:04.473 --> 00:00:05.113
Let’s go this way.

3
00:00:41.468 --> 00:00:42.969
Brad: The guards are everywhere.

4
00:00:42.989 --> 00:00:47.851
Danny: If only they would move somewhere else.

5
00:00:48.451 --> 00:00:48.991
Brad: That’s it!

6
00:00:49.011 --> 00:00:49.531
Danny: What?

7
00:00:51.152 --> 00:00:54.493
Brad: We could make a noise back near the gate.

8
00:00:54.513 --> 00:00:57.495
Brad: Maybe the guards will run to see what it is.

9
00:00:57.515 --> 00:00:59.715
Danny: Great idea.

10
00:01:00.476 --> 00:01:01.856
One of us could throw a pebble.

11
00:01:01.876 --> 00:01:04.998
Brad: All the pebbles are bigger than us.

12
00:01:05.998 --> 00:01:07.799
But this grain of sand should work.

13
00:01:08.459 --> 00:01:09.800
Brad: Who has the strongest arm?

14
00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:11.260
Danny: Tina.

15
00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.883
Brad: Well, she’s not here.

16
00:01:14.903 --> 00:01:16.765
Danny: I know.

17
00:01:17.706 --> 00:01:19.187
We’ll have to throw it together.

18
00:01:19.207 --> 00:01:22.149
Brad: Teamwork always works for us.

19
00:01:28.654 --> 00:01:31.096
One, two Danny: Three!

20
00:01:32.337 --> 00:01:37.962
Mite 1: Hey!

21
00:01:38.002 --> 00:01:38.782
Did you hear that?

22
00:01:38.802 --> 00:01:40.484
Mite 2: We should check it out!

23
00:01:41.036 --> 00:01:42.357
Mite 1: Get the other guards!

24
00:01:48.841 --> 00:01:50.402
Perfect! Let’s go!

25
00:01:51.263 --> 00:01:53.484
It won’t be long before the guards come back.

26
00:01:54.005 --> 00:01:55.886
Danny: I see some bottle caps.

27
00:01:56.767 --> 00:01:58.108
Maybe we could stack them.

28
00:01:58.128 --> 00:02:00.189
Brad: It’s worth a try.

29
00:02:07.314 --> 00:02:08.755
This isn’t going to work.

30
00:02:09.976 --> 00:02:11.937
Danny: Hey, there’s a straw over there.

31
00:02:11.957 --> 00:02:14.178
Brad: How big?

32
00:02:14.198 --> 00:02:16.759
Danny: It’s a regular-size straw.

33
00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:18.160
It’s big!

34
00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:22.762
Brad: Geez, I never thought a straw could look so big!

35
00:02:22.782 --> 00:02:26.224
Danny: It’s long enough to reach the top of the wall.

36
00:02:26.244 --> 00:02:29.106
Brad: Do you think we can lift it?

37
00:02:29.126 --> 00:02:33.428
Danny: That’s the great thing about straws: they’re light.

38
00:02:42.288 --> 00:02:43.889
Brad: Careful, careful.

39
00:02:47.011 --> 00:02:48.311
Brad: Okay, now turn it.

40
00:02:50.873 --> 00:02:54.615
Danny: There, we did it!

41
00:02:55.495 --> 00:02:57.136
Brad: Okay, I’m going to climb up.

42
00:02:58.117 --> 00:02:58.617
Danny: You?

43
00:02:59.257 --> 00:03:00.778
But you’re not good at climbing!

44
00:03:00.798 --> 00:03:04.200
Brad: You just hold it steady.

45
00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:06.181
Danny: Are you sure?

46
00:03:06.201 --> 00:03:08.482
It looks very slippery.

47
00:03:08.502 --> 00:03:11.844
Brad: If Tina were here, she would climb it.

48
00:03:12.376 --> 00:03:13.656
But it’s just you and me.

49
00:03:13.676 --> 00:03:15.197
Danny: Okay.

50
00:03:15.437 --> 00:03:16.297
Give it a try.

51
00:03:16.317 --> 00:03:19.458
Danny: Careful!

52
00:03:19.478 --> 00:03:20.939
Brad: I’m okay.

53
00:03:20.959 --> 00:03:25.960
Danny: What do you see?

54
00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:32.042
Brad: There are several towers and lots of mites!

55
00:03:32.062 --> 00:03:34.863
Danny: Any sign of Chuck and Dave?

56
00:03:35.884 --> 00:03:42.257
Brad: I’m looking Brad: Oh no!

57
00:03:42.277 --> 00:03:43.801
Danny: What?

58
00:03:43.821 --> 00:03:46.006
Brad: They’re in a prison.

59
00:03:46.868 --> 00:03:48.211
We’ll never get them out!
